## Vendored code

`lib/linter.py` is vendored and adapted from `evals/ste_lint.py` in
https://github.com/AminBlg/SimpleEnglish at commit
59bf6702197a5aadc96d197ea17f290d8d50dcd3.

The whitespace tokenizer, sentence splitter, exclusion approach and
line-oriented reporting come from that implementation. CopyDesk replaces its
ASD-STE100 rule list, and deliberately drops the upstream bans on
contractions, modal verbs and semicolons.

The full notice travels in the file's own header and is repeated here.

